title: NightSpire Ransomware Pre-Encryption Exfiltration via Rclone or MEGACmd
id: 2f780111-8454-444e-bebc-4fe01fc41952
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects execution of the data-transfer tooling NightSpire affiliates use to
    exfiltrate victim data before deploying the Go-based encryptor. Proven
    Data's NightSpire analysis documents data moved to attacker-controlled
    infrastructure with WinSCP, MEGACmd, or Rclone ahead of encryption; this
    rule targets the rarer rclone and MEGACmd binaries for precision. The
    subsequent encryptor is obfuscated with RC4/XOR and sleeps between
    encryption passes to evade real-time detection.
references:
    - https://www.provendata.com/blog/nightspire-ransomware
    - https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/nightspire-ransomware-attack-chain-tools-and-tactics
    - https://www.huntress.com/blog/nightspire-ransomware
    - https://ransomware.ninja/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-07
tags:
    - attack.t1567
    - attack.exfiltration
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_exfil_tools:
        Image|contains:
            - 'rclone'
            - 'MEGACmd'
            - 'MEGAcmd'
    condition: selection_exfil_tools
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate administrators using rclone for backup or replication jobs
    - End users running the MEGACmd desktop sync client for MEGA storage
level: medium
